 "notes": [
  "Source PDF has two parts: (1) an original members list grouped under section headings 'EAST BENGAL-44', 'WEST PUNJAB', 'NORTH-WEST FRONTIER PROVINCE-3', 'SINDH-4', 'BALUCHISTAN-1'; and (2) a 'CHANGES MEMBERS FIRST CONSTITUTE ASSEMBLY FROM JULY 1949-1954' list of members who joined/replaced others over time, grouped by month/year.",
  "Only an S.No and permanent-address column are given, no explicit seat/constituency code and no party column; seat/raw_constituency are null for the original-list members. For the 'changes' list, the place name given in the address column is preserved in raw_constituency, but province is left null because no section heading groups these entries by province.",
  "Numbering gaps in the original list (item numbers 58-61 and 68 have no printed name) mean the section headings' stated totals (e.g. 'SINDH-4') exceed the number of members actually printed; only printed names were transcribed. Original-list total transcribed: 64 members (East Bengal 44, West Punjab 13, NWFP 3, Sindh 3, Baluchistan 1).",
  "'Changes' list total transcribed: 31 members (one 'NOVEMBER, 1950' batch is marked 'NIL' in the source and yields no member).",
  "This was a Constituent Assembly whose members were elected indirectly by the provincial legislatures, not by direct general franchise; elected_via is set to 'indirect' for the original list and 'by_election' for the later 'changes' list entries (replacements/co-options over the assembly's life), per the PDF's own framing.",
  "The PDF contains no separate reserved women's or minority/non-Muslim seat heading; all entries are recorded as seat_type 'general'. (A small number of named individuals, e.g. Begum Shaista Suhrawardy Ikramullah and Begum Jahan Ara Shah Nawaz, were women members, but the source does not group them under a distinct reserved-seat heading, so seat_type is left 'general' per the extraction rule.)",
  "OCR text had scattered stray spaces inside words (e.g. 'Moham m ad'); these were collapsed to normal spelling without otherwise altering names.",
  "Total members recorded for Assembly 1: 95 (64 original + 31 from the changes list)."
 ],
